    <!-- Mirror - Actionable error cards. Copy is the design's verbatim err-adb / err-nodevice /
         err-multi text (inputs/design-error-states.md), except err-multi's second sentence:
         the design promises "Rectify remembers it until you quit", which is false against
         sessionDeviceId (nulled by onSessionLost, selectPlatform and stopSession), so the
         shipped sentence claims only the session. Same rule as mirror_waiting_subtitle. -->
    <string name="mirror_error_tool_missing_title">adb isn\'t on your PATH</string>
    <string name="mirror_error_tool_missing_body">Rectify uses Android platform-tools to find devices. Install them, or point Rectify at an adb you already have.</string>
    <string name="mirror_error_no_device_title">No Android device detected</string>
    <string name="mirror_error_no_device_body">adb is running but sees nothing. On the phone, turn on USB debugging and tap Allow on the prompt.</string>
    <!-- No design state exists for a failed poll (it is Android-only). The copy has to say adb
         itself did not answer, never that the bench is empty, or the card misreports (FR-32). -->
    <string name="mirror_error_poll_failed_title">adb stopped responding</string>
    <string name="mirror_error_poll_failed_body">The device poll never came back, so nothing is known about what is attached. Retry, or read what adb reported in the footer.</string>
